    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f57eb85b_41fd4689",
        "filename": "include/linux/lsm_hooks.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1332,
      "author": {
        "id": 1082649
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-17T21:51:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Normally LSM hooks are added to manage _objects_, not syscalls. So, something like map creation and usage (i.e. one hook for creation, one hook for usage). The usage hook would be called during map_lookup_elem, map_update_elem, map_delete_elem, map_get_next_key, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "89a1fa24_524a388a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1332,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1332,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "1068446183aa820f0609c369a0c967171b331fe3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c925cb75_921a561e",
        "filename": "include/linux/lsm_hooks.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1332,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-17T22:34:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed.\n\nLet\u0027s determine the objects that we care about e.g.\n1. bpf_map\n2. bpf_prog\n\nthe permissions that we care about for each object:\n1. bpf_map\n   create\n   update\n   delete\n   use (group non-sensitive permissions together here)\n2. bpf_prog\n   load\n   use (attach and detach, since granting one and not the other doesn\u0027t make sense)",
      "parentUuid": "f57eb85b_41fd4689",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1332,
        "startChar": 3,
